WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.419
Relative pronouns. The
one who, the thing which.

2
00:00:03.869 --> 00:00:06.287
In English we say: the student who passed.

3
00:00:06.437 --> 00:00:10.567
Here, the little word, who, joins
the noun to a short clause about it.

4
00:00:10.567 --> 00:00:12.042
It is a relative pronoun.

5
00:00:12.192 --> 00:00:16.568
In Arabic, a relative pronoun is
fixed. Its ending does not change.

6
00:00:16.568 --> 00:00:21.270
The only exception is a pair of words
for two. They come in chapter six.

7
00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:25.107
And it never stands alone. A
clause always comes after it.

8
00:00:25.657 --> 00:00:27.665
Chapter one. The table to learn.

9
00:00:28.015 --> 00:00:30.101
Here are the relatives to learn by heart.

10
00:00:30.351 --> 00:00:33.211
The first one is for one
male, or one masculine thing.

11
00:00:33.461 --> 00:00:34.376
‫الَّذِي‬

12
00:00:34.726 --> 00:00:36.014
The student who passed.

13
00:00:36.264 --> 00:00:38.681
‫الطَّالِبُ الَّذِي نَجَحَ‬

14
00:00:39.131 --> 00:00:42.310
The second one is for one
female, or one feminine thing.

15
00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:43.443
‫الَّتِي‬

16
00:00:43.793 --> 00:00:44.945
The girl who passed.

17
00:00:45.195 --> 00:00:47.608
‫الْبِنْتُ الَّتِي نَجَحَتْ‬

18
00:00:48.058 --> 00:00:49.964
The third one is for a group of males.

19
00:00:50.214 --> 00:00:51.164
‫الَّذِينَ‬

20
00:00:51.514 --> 00:00:52.819
The students who passed.

21
00:00:53.069 --> 00:00:55.925
‫الطُّلَّابُ الَّذِينَ نَجَحُوا‬

22
00:00:56.375 --> 00:01:01.145
The last row is for a group of females.
It has two words, and both are correct.

23
00:01:01.395 --> 00:01:02.471
‫اللَّاتِي‬

24
00:01:02.721 --> 00:01:03.954
‫اللَّوَاتِي‬

25
00:01:04.304 --> 00:01:05.649
The women who passed.

26
00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:08.745
‫النِّسَاءُ اللَّاتِي نَجَحْنَ‬

27
00:01:09.195 --> 00:01:12.352
In every example, the relative
comes right after the noun.

28
00:01:12.902 --> 00:01:16.800
Next, two relatives that are
general. No noun comes before them.

29
00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:19.626
The first means the one
who. It is for people.

30
00:01:19.876 --> 00:01:20.597
‫مَنْ‬

31
00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:22.327
The one who passed came.

32
00:01:22.577 --> 00:01:24.403
‫جَاءَ مَنْ نَجَحَ‬

33
00:01:24.853 --> 00:01:27.212
The second means what. It is for things.

34
00:01:27.462 --> 00:01:28.177
‫مَا‬

35
00:01:28.527 --> 00:01:30.005
I read what the teacher wrote.

36
00:01:30.255 --> 00:01:33.151
‫قَرَأْتُ مَا كَتَبَ الْمُدَرِّسُ‬

37
00:01:33.701 --> 00:01:38.542
A tip on spelling. These three are written
with a single L, with a shadda on it.

38
00:01:38.792 --> 00:01:39.707
‫الَّذِي‬

39
00:01:39.907 --> 00:01:40.790
‫الَّتِي‬

40
00:01:40.990 --> 00:01:41.940
‫الَّذِينَ‬

41
00:01:42.290 --> 00:01:45.778
The two words for a group of females
are written with the L twice.

42
00:01:46.028 --> 00:01:47.104
‫اللَّاتِي‬

43
00:01:47.304 --> 00:01:48.537
‫اللَّوَاتِي‬

44
00:01:49.087 --> 00:01:51.322
Now the rule. All of these are fixed.

45
00:01:51.572 --> 00:01:53.521
Look at the word for a group of males.

46
00:01:53.771 --> 00:01:54.721
‫الَّذِينَ‬

47
00:01:55.071 --> 00:01:57.739
It ends like a plural.
But it never changes.

48
00:01:57.889 --> 00:02:00.653
In rafʿ, in naṣb and in
jarr, it stays the same.

49
00:02:00.903 --> 00:02:01.853
‫الَّذِينَ‬

50
00:02:02.203 --> 00:02:04.510
And these two always
end in a long ī sound.

51
00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:05.675
‫الَّذِي‬

52
00:02:05.875 --> 00:02:06.758
‫الَّتِي‬

53
00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:12.062
Chapter two. A relative
needs a clause after it.

54
00:02:12.412 --> 00:02:14.136
This word alone means nothing.

55
00:02:14.386 --> 00:02:15.301
‫الَّذِي‬

56
00:02:15.651 --> 00:02:17.858
The one who did what? We wait for more.

57
00:02:18.208 --> 00:02:22.818
The clause after it completes its
meaning. This clause is called the ṣila.

58
00:02:23.068 --> 00:02:23.952
‫صِلَةٌ‬

59
00:02:24.502 --> 00:02:26.790
First. The student who passed came.

60
00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:30.026
‫جَاءَ الطَّالِبُ الَّذِي نَجَحَ‬

61
00:02:30.476 --> 00:02:33.091
The ṣila is just the
verb. It means he passed.

62
00:02:33.341 --> 00:02:34.182
‫نَجَحَ‬

63
00:02:34.632 --> 00:02:37.347
Second. This is the girl
who wrote the lesson.

64
00:02:37.597 --> 00:02:42.384
‫هَذِهِ هِيَ الْبِنْتُ‬
‫الَّتِي كَتَبَتِ الدَّرْسَ‬

65
00:02:42.834 --> 00:02:44.636
The ṣila means she wrote the lesson.

66
00:02:44.886 --> 00:02:46.673
‫كَتَبَتِ الدَّرْسَ‬

67
00:02:47.123 --> 00:02:49.694
Third. The book which
is on the desk is new.

68
00:02:49.944 --> 00:02:54.053
‫الْكِتَابُ الَّذِي عَلَى‬
‫الْمَكْتَبِ جَدِيدٌ‬

69
00:02:54.503 --> 00:02:58.383
Here the ṣila has no verb. It
is a place phrase: on the desk.

70
00:02:58.633 --> 00:03:00.212
‫عَلَى الْمَكْتَبِ‬

71
00:03:00.662 --> 00:03:03.363
Fourth. The men who sat
in the mosque went out.

72
00:03:03.613 --> 00:03:09.041
‫خَرَجَ الرِّجَالُ الَّذِينَ‬
‫جَلَسُوا فِي الْمَسْجِدِ‬

73
00:03:09.491 --> 00:03:11.379
The ṣila means they sat in the mosque.

74
00:03:11.629 --> 00:03:14.113
‫جَلَسُوا فِي الْمَسْجِدِ‬

75
00:03:14.763 --> 00:03:17.831
A tip. The ṣila has a small
link back to the noun.

76
00:03:18.081 --> 00:03:19.917
Often the link is hidden in the verb.

77
00:03:20.167 --> 00:03:21.008
‫نَجَحَ‬

78
00:03:21.358 --> 00:03:24.590
This verb means he passed.
The hidden he is the student.

79
00:03:24.940 --> 00:03:29.585
Sometimes the link is an attached
pronoun. The student whose house is near.

80
00:03:29.835 --> 00:03:33.439
‫الطَّالِبُ الَّذِي بَيْتُهُ قَرِيبٌ‬

81
00:03:33.889 --> 00:03:37.756
The small ending on house means
his. It points back to the student.

82
00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:42.715
Chapter three. Choose
by the noun before it.

83
00:03:43.065 --> 00:03:46.895
A relative works like an adjective.
It follows a noun with al.

84
00:03:47.045 --> 00:03:50.878
And it matches that noun. Male
or female. One or a group.

85
00:03:51.428 --> 00:03:52.932
The boy who is in the house.

86
00:03:53.182 --> 00:03:56.046
‫الْوَلَدُ الَّذِي فِي الْبَيْتِ‬

87
00:03:56.496 --> 00:03:59.066
The boy is one male.
So we choose this one.

88
00:03:59.316 --> 00:04:00.231
‫الَّذِي‬

89
00:04:00.681 --> 00:04:02.234
The watch which is on the bed.

90
00:04:02.484 --> 00:04:05.856
‫السَّاعَةُ الَّتِي عَلَى السَّرِيرِ‬

91
00:04:06.306 --> 00:04:07.932
The word for watch is feminine.

92
00:04:08.182 --> 00:04:09.320
‫السَّاعَةُ‬

93
00:04:09.670 --> 00:04:13.002
It is a thing, but a feminine
one. So we choose this one.

94
00:04:13.252 --> 00:04:14.135
‫الَّتِي‬

95
00:04:14.585 --> 00:04:15.968
The boys who went out.

96
00:04:16.218 --> 00:04:18.995
‫الْأَوْلَادُ الَّذِينَ خَرَجُوا‬

97
00:04:19.445 --> 00:04:21.838
A group of males. So we choose this one.

98
00:04:22.088 --> 00:04:23.038
‫الَّذِينَ‬

99
00:04:23.488 --> 00:04:24.778
The women who went out.

100
00:04:25.028 --> 00:04:27.899
‫النِّسَاءُ اللَّاتِي خَرَجْنَ‬

101
00:04:28.349 --> 00:04:30.913
A group of females. So we choose this one.

102
00:04:31.163 --> 00:04:32.239
‫اللَّاتِي‬

103
00:04:32.889 --> 00:04:37.558
Two tips. First, look at the verb in
the ṣila too. It matches the relative.

104
00:04:37.808 --> 00:04:39.908
For one male, the verb means he went out.

105
00:04:40.158 --> 00:04:41.537
‫الَّذِي خَرَجَ‬

106
00:04:41.887 --> 00:04:43.468
For one female, she went out.

107
00:04:43.718 --> 00:04:45.321
‫الَّتِي خَرَجَتْ‬

108
00:04:45.671 --> 00:04:47.451
For a group of males, they went out.

109
00:04:47.701 --> 00:04:49.482
‫الَّذِينَ خَرَجُوا‬

110
00:04:49.832 --> 00:04:52.548
For a group of females, the
verb has its own ending.

111
00:04:52.798 --> 00:04:54.592
‫اللَّاتِي خَرَجْنَ‬

112
00:04:55.142 --> 00:04:59.410
Second. After a noun without al,
Arabic leaves the relative out.

113
00:04:59.660 --> 00:05:01.174
A student who passed came.

114
00:05:01.424 --> 00:05:03.438
‫جَاءَ طَالِبٌ نَجَحَ‬

115
00:05:03.888 --> 00:05:07.098
Here student has no al. So
no relative comes after it.

116
00:05:07.348 --> 00:05:12.105
In English we still say who. In Arabic,
the clause comes straight after the noun.

117
00:05:14.467 --> 00:05:15.441
Chapter four.

118
00:05:15.591 --> 00:05:16.312
‫مَنْ‬

119
00:05:16.462 --> 00:05:17.108
and

120
00:05:17.158 --> 00:05:17.873
‫مَا‬

121
00:05:18.123 --> 00:05:19.391
Question or relative?

122
00:05:19.841 --> 00:05:22.150
These two words are also question words.

123
00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:24.805
You learn them as question
words in unit five.

124
00:05:25.055 --> 00:05:27.918
So how do we tell them
apart? Look at the sentence.

125
00:05:28.168 --> 00:05:29.951
A question ends in a question mark.

126
00:05:30.101 --> 00:05:34.396
A relative sits inside a normal
sentence. It means the one who, or what.

127
00:05:34.946 --> 00:05:35.836
Who passed?

128
00:05:36.086 --> 00:05:37.341
‫مَنْ نَجَحَ‬

129
00:05:37.691 --> 00:05:40.538
It ends in a question mark.
So this is a question.

130
00:05:40.988 --> 00:05:42.368
The one who passed came.

131
00:05:42.618 --> 00:05:44.444
‫جَاءَ مَنْ نَجَحَ‬

132
00:05:44.794 --> 00:05:49.684
This is a normal sentence. So the word
is a relative here. It means the one who.

133
00:05:49.934 --> 00:05:52.464
Its ṣila is the verb. It means he passed.

134
00:05:52.714 --> 00:05:53.555
‫نَجَحَ‬

135
00:05:54.005 --> 00:05:55.188
What is on the desk?

136
00:05:55.438 --> 00:05:57.510
‫مَا عَلَى الْمَكْتَبِ‬

137
00:05:57.860 --> 00:06:00.481
Again, a question mark.
So it is a question.

138
00:06:00.931 --> 00:06:02.313
Read what is on the desk.

139
00:06:02.563 --> 00:06:05.496
‫اِقْرَأْ مَا عَلَى الْمَكْتَبِ‬

140
00:06:05.846 --> 00:06:10.299
This is an order, with no question
mark. So the word is a relative here.

141
00:06:10.299 --> 00:06:11.165
It means what.

142
00:06:13.500 --> 00:06:15.841
Chapter five. Its place in the sentence.

143
00:06:16.191 --> 00:06:18.840
A relative after a noun
works like an adjective.

144
00:06:18.990 --> 00:06:23.394
An adjective copies the ending of
its noun. But a relative is fixed.

145
00:06:23.394 --> 00:06:25.078
It cannot copy the ending.

146
00:06:25.328 --> 00:06:29.258
So it copies the place of the noun
before it: rafʿ, naṣb or jarr.

147
00:06:29.258 --> 00:06:30.890
Its ending does not change.

148
00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:32.937
The student who passed came.

149
00:06:33.187 --> 00:06:36.173
‫جَاءَ الطَّالِبُ الَّذِي نَجَحَ‬

150
00:06:36.623 --> 00:06:39.364
The student is the doer.
It is rafʿ, with damma.

151
00:06:39.614 --> 00:06:40.961
‫الطَّالِبُ‬

152
00:06:41.311 --> 00:06:43.377
So the relative is in the place of rafʿ.

153
00:06:43.627 --> 00:06:44.542
‫الَّذِي‬

154
00:06:45.092 --> 00:06:47.296
The principal thanked
the student who passed.

155
00:06:47.546 --> 00:06:51.480
‫شَكَرَ الْمُدِيرُ‬
‫الطَّالِبَ الَّذِي نَجَحَ‬

156
00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:55.111
Now the student is the object.
It is naṣb, with fatha.

157
00:06:55.361 --> 00:06:56.530
‫الطَّالِبَ‬

158
00:06:56.880 --> 00:07:00.826
So the relative is in the place of
naṣb. Its ending stays the same.

159
00:07:01.076 --> 00:07:01.991
‫الَّذِي‬

160
00:07:02.541 --> 00:07:04.280
I went to the student who passed.

161
00:07:04.530 --> 00:07:08.974
‫ذَهَبْتُ إِلَى الطَّالِبِ الَّذِي نَجَحَ‬

162
00:07:09.424 --> 00:07:13.657
Now the student comes after a
preposition. It is jarr, with kasra.

163
00:07:13.907 --> 00:07:15.230
‫الطَّالِبِ‬

164
00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:20.061
So the relative is in the place of
jarr. Again, its ending stays the same.

165
00:07:20.311 --> 00:07:21.226
‫الَّذِي‬

166
00:07:21.876 --> 00:07:24.840
A tip. The two general
relatives stand alone.

167
00:07:25.090 --> 00:07:25.811
‫مَنْ‬

168
00:07:26.011 --> 00:07:26.726
‫مَا‬

169
00:07:27.076 --> 00:07:30.481
Stand alone means only that
no noun comes before them.

170
00:07:30.481 --> 00:07:32.372
A ṣila still comes after them.

171
00:07:32.522 --> 00:07:34.928
With no noun to copy,
they have their own job.

172
00:07:35.178 --> 00:07:36.558
The one who passed came.

173
00:07:36.808 --> 00:07:38.634
‫جَاءَ مَنْ نَجَحَ‬

174
00:07:39.084 --> 00:07:39.962
Who came?

175
00:07:40.312 --> 00:07:43.011
The one who passed. So
this word is the doer.

176
00:07:43.261 --> 00:07:43.982
‫مَنْ‬

177
00:07:44.332 --> 00:07:48.621
The doer takes rafʿ. This word is
fixed, so it is in the place of rafʿ.

178
00:07:50.967 --> 00:07:52.690
Chapter six. Not fixed.

179
00:07:52.940 --> 00:07:54.022
‫اللَّذَانِ‬

180
00:07:54.172 --> 00:07:54.818
and

181
00:07:54.868 --> 00:07:55.952
‫اللَّتَانِ‬

182
00:07:56.502 --> 00:08:00.840
Careful. Two more relatives mean
the two who. And these words change.

183
00:08:01.090 --> 00:08:02.620
This one is for two males.

184
00:08:02.870 --> 00:08:03.952
‫اللَّذَانِ‬

185
00:08:04.302 --> 00:08:05.824
This one is for two females.

186
00:08:06.074 --> 00:08:07.158
‫اللَّتَانِ‬

187
00:08:07.508 --> 00:08:10.074
These two are not fixed.
They are flexible.

188
00:08:10.324 --> 00:08:12.385
In naṣb and jarr, they become these.

189
00:08:12.635 --> 00:08:14.078
‫اللَّذَيْنِ‬

190
00:08:14.278 --> 00:08:15.512
‫اللَّتَيْنِ‬

191
00:08:15.962 --> 00:08:18.208
You learn them with the dual in Stage 4.

192
00:08:18.458 --> 00:08:19.888
Here they are as a table.

193
00:08:20.138 --> 00:08:22.494
In rafʿ, for two males
and for two females.

194
00:08:22.744 --> 00:08:23.826
‫اللَّذَانِ‬

195
00:08:24.026 --> 00:08:25.110
‫اللَّتَانِ‬

196
00:08:25.460 --> 00:08:28.359
In naṣb and jarr, for two
males and for two females.

197
00:08:28.609 --> 00:08:30.052
‫اللَّذَيْنِ‬

198
00:08:30.252 --> 00:08:31.486
‫اللَّتَيْنِ‬

199
00:08:31.836 --> 00:08:33.347
For now, know that they change.

200
00:08:33.997 --> 00:08:34.849
In short.

201
00:08:35.199 --> 00:08:36.966
One. For one male or thing.

202
00:08:37.116 --> 00:08:38.031
‫الَّذِي‬

203
00:08:38.281 --> 00:08:39.699
For one female or thing.

204
00:08:39.949 --> 00:08:40.832
‫الَّتِي‬

205
00:08:41.082 --> 00:08:41.981
For males.

206
00:08:42.231 --> 00:08:43.181
‫الَّذِينَ‬

207
00:08:43.431 --> 00:08:44.318
For females.

208
00:08:44.568 --> 00:08:45.644
‫اللَّاتِي‬

209
00:08:45.794 --> 00:08:47.027
‫اللَّوَاتِي‬

210
00:08:47.477 --> 00:08:49.438
Two. The one who, for people.

211
00:08:49.588 --> 00:08:50.309
‫مَنْ‬

212
00:08:50.559 --> 00:08:51.632
What, for things.

213
00:08:51.882 --> 00:08:52.597
‫مَا‬

214
00:08:53.047 --> 00:08:55.662
Three. A relative needs a ṣila after it.

215
00:08:55.812 --> 00:08:56.696
‫صِلَةٌ‬

216
00:08:56.946 --> 00:08:58.231
The one who passed.

217
00:08:58.381 --> 00:08:59.919
‫الَّذِي نَجَحَ‬

218
00:09:00.369 --> 00:09:02.335
Four. Match the noun before it.

219
00:09:02.485 --> 00:09:06.302
The relative copies the place of
that noun: rafʿ, naṣb or jarr.

